# Host cron of user exedev on the exe.dev VM. Install (replaces the whole crontab): crontab deploy/crontab
# Check:  crontab -l     Log: data/purge_inbox.log (gitignored)
#
# Weekly, Sunday 12:00 UTC (after the nightly pass 03:00-~09:45 and the verify that queues behind it):
# keep the last 4 days of raw crawler rows in data/inbox.sqlite (= the last 4 nightly runs, ~100 MB each).
# Older rows live on only in crawl_output/run_<id>.jsonl. Nothing else touches the queue's size.
0 12 * * 0 cd /home/exedev/repo && .venv/bin/python -m pflege_jobs.cli purge-inbox --days 4 >> data/purge_inbox.log 2>&1
#
# Daily, 12:05 UTC (after the nightly pass and its verify): gzip the dump of every run that is finished (~110 MB -> ~16 MB
# each, Ivan 2026-10-08: whatever is not read and can be compressed is compressed, always). tools/compress_crawl_output.py reads
# crawl_runs, leaves running and queued runs plain, checks the .gz line for line before it replaces the file, deletes no row;
# a run unknown to crawl_runs, an existing .gz or a failed read-back are printed as PROBLEM and exit 1. app/hunter.py and
# tools/task95_replay.py read the .gz.
5 12 * * * cd /home/exedev/repo && .venv/bin/python tools/compress_crawl_output.py --apply >> data/purge_inbox.log 2>&1
